  "law": [
    "A face with fewer than three corners never makes subdivision refuse the mesh; the rest of the mesh is refined exactly as without that face, one undo entry.",
    "A selected (or, with nothing selected, any) two-corner face is replaced by two two-corner faces through a split vertex; both carry the face's selection.",
    "In the default mode the split vertex is the edge point an earlier refined face of three or more corners created for the same vertex pair; otherwise it is a new vertex at the midpoint of the pair's original positions. In the flat and smooth modes it is the edge point of any refined face on that pair, whichever face comes first. Endpoints move only as the faces of three or more corners that use them move.",
    "An unselected two-corner face is carried through unchanged, also when a refined face splits its edge; the other faces on that edge take the edge point, the two-corner face does not.",
    "Splitting a selected two-corner face never changes the unselected faces that share its edge.",
    "The same holds for the flat and smooth modes (topology; smooth positions of other vertices are not compared).",
    "The subpatch toggle works face by face and is not refused: a two-corner face that is not subpatch stays as it is, and a two-corner face that is subpatch becomes plain in the same press as the other faces change."
  ],
  "reads": {
    "mesh": "model {v,e,f}",
